Error [E0904]: Can't figure out what `T` should be here
  --> tests/ui/generic_infer_fail.jet:3:12
    |
  3 | fn run() { empty_list() }
    |            ^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Generic calls need enough context to pick a concrete type
 Fix: Pass the type argument explicitly, like `make<Int>()`, or give the value a typed head, like `p :: Pair<Int>{ … }`
